  "name": "paper-cut",
  "vibe": "Cream (#f4e9dc) with coral (#e2654e), teal (#2f8f83) and mustard (#e8b23c) — notably, it rotates full-bleed colour fields, dropping statement onto coral, montage onto teal, stats onto ink and the CTA onto mustard, so the film changes paper stock as it goes. Shrikhand, a fat display serif, is the only serif in the set; Sen carries the body. The world is three torn-paper wave bands stacked at 62%, 72% and 84% of the height, each breathing up and down on its own slow sine so the layers lift against one another, plus a two-tone paper sun (coral disc, mustard core) at upper right and nine rounded offcuts drifting and spinning continuously. Cards are matte paper sheets with ink outlines; chips are squares. Drag-to-assemble is its signature. For craft brands, zines, studios, kids and print-led makers.",
